 ```
 
 ## Why this shape
@@ -44,6 +45,27 @@ Docker on the VM
   same separation in dev means there's no "but it worked on my
   laptop" rewrite when the deploy story comes around.
 
+* **Argos as a local sidecar** keeps per-channel YouTube descriptions off
+  NVIDIA. During posting, NVIDIA supplies the localized title and Argos
+  supplies the localized description; the worker waits for Argos to become
+  healthy before starting.
+
+Argos is built from `ops/argos` and downloads the language models into the
+`instaedit_argos_packages` named volume on first start. The default endpoint
+is already present in `.env.dev`:
+
+```text
+ARGOS_TRANSLATE_URL=http://argos:5003/translate
+```
+
+To build or restart only the sidecar:
+
+```bash
+INSTAEDIT_ENV_FILE=.env.dev docker compose --env-file .env.dev \
+  -f docker-compose.yml -f docker-compose.local.yml up -d --build argos
+curl http://127.0.0.1:5003/health
+```
+
